# Analytics Rules

> *Analytics Rules are the core detection mechanism in Microsoft Sentinel, converting KQL queries into automated security alerts.*

---

# Overview

Analytics Rules continuously evaluate security telemetry to identify suspicious or malicious activity. They automate threat detection by executing Kusto Query Language (KQL) queries on a scheduled basis and generating alerts when defined conditions are met.

Effective Analytics Rules combine accurate detection logic, appropriate thresholds, entity mapping, and alert tuning to minimize false positives while ensuring important security events are detected.

This section demonstrates how the SSH brute-force detection developed throughout this handbook is deployed as a Scheduled Analytics Rule.

